IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vic-nouns`
IMPORT `vic-definitions`

-- Hand-written cases for the definitions: the lookup by section, the contrary intention, a closed list ("means") and an open list ("includes").
-- Each expected value is written by hand from the definition named beside it.

§ `Lookups`

-- s 38: the term Imperial Act is defined; s 38 begins "unless the contrary intention appears", so with a contrary intention the text gives no meaning.
#ASSERT `meaning of a term defined in a section` "s 38" "Imperial Act" FALSE EQUALS JUST `s38 definition 054 of Imperial Act`
#ASSERT `meaning of a term defined in a section` "s 38" "Imperial Act" TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A term the section does not define.
#ASSERT `meaning of a term defined in a section` "s 38" "amended" FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3 defines amended, made and repealed (for subordinate instruments); s 38 does not.
#ASSERT `kind of the definition of a term` "s 3" "amended" FALSE EQUALS JUST VicIncludes
#ASSERT `wording of the definition of a term` "s 3" "made" FALSE EQUALS JUST "issued or granted;"
#ASSERT `kind of the definition of a term` "s 3" "repealed" TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The sections that continue s 38 apply in all Acts and subordinate instruments; s 3, s 60, s 64A(3) and s 64B(1) do not.
#ASSERT `meaning of a term in all Acts and subordinate instruments` "Imperial Act" FALSE EQUALS JUST `s38 definition 054 of Imperial Act`
#ASSERT `meaning of a term in all Acts and subordinate instruments` "Imperial Act" TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `meaning of a term in all Acts and subordinate instruments` "amended" FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `meaning of a term in all Acts and subordinate instruments` "authorised version" FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `meaning of a term in all Acts and subordinate instruments` "non-citizen" FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The same term defined in two sections: the lookup by section returns each section's own definition.
#ASSERT `kind of the definition of a term` "s 64A(3)" "non-citizen" FALSE EQUALS JUST VicIncludes
#ASSERT `kind of the definition of a term` "s 64B(1)" "non-citizen" FALSE EQUALS JUST VicHasTheSameMeaningAs

§ `Closed and open lists`

-- Imperial Act means an Act passed by one of four Parliaments: the list is closed ("means"), so another Parliament's Act is not within it.
#ASSERT `thing is within the term as defined` "s 38" "Imperial Act" "the Parliament of Great Britain" FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `thing is within the term as defined` "s 38" "Imperial Act" "the Parliament of England" FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `thing is within the term as defined` "s 38" "Imperial Act" "the Parliament of Victoria" FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The contrary intention appears: the text gives no meaning, so nothing is said about whether the thing is within it.
#ASSERT `thing is within the term as defined` "s 38" "Imperial Act" "the Parliament of Great Britain" TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- document includes, in addition to a document in writing, a list of things: a listed thing is within the term; the text does not say that anything else is outside it.
#ASSERT `thing is within the term as defined` "s 38" "document" "any photograph" FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `thing is within the term as defined` "s 38" "document" "a spoken promise" FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- amended includes altered or varied (for a subordinate instrument); the definition names no list of members, so nothing is said of a particular thing.
#ASSERT `thing is within the term as defined` "s 3" "amended" "altered" FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A term not defined at all.
#ASSERT `thing is within the term as defined` "s 38" "marmalade" "orange" FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Pointing definitions`

-- Australian lawyer has the same meaning as it has in the Legal Profession Uniform Law (Victoria): the Act points outside the sources.
#ASSERT `kind of the definition of a term` "s 38" "Australian lawyer" FALSE EQUALS JUST VicHasTheSameMeaningAs
#ASSERT `wording of the definition of a term` "s 38" "Australian lawyer" FALSE EQUALS JUST "as it has in the Legal Profession Uniform Law (Victoria);"
